Final Checklist - FTC Identity Theft Complaint
Requesting Party: ____________________
Execution
• The complaint letter must be signed. Witnessing or notarization is not required.
Supporting Documentation
• Attach copies of all relevant documents supporting the identity theft claim, where applicable.
Copies
• Send the original signed letter to the Federal Trade Commission.
• Submit copies of supporting documents unless an original is specifically required.
• Retain a complete copy of the letter and all enclosures for your records. If an original document is submitted, keep a copy.
Additional Guidance
• Although not mandatory, sending the letter via a trackable delivery method (e.g., certified mail with return receipt requested or overnight courier) is strongly recommended.
• After a reasonable period, follow up to confirm that the complaint has been received and appropriately processed.
